        <mxCell id="n37" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F7F7F7;strokeColor=#8A8A8A;strokeWidth=2;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;arcSize=16;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 17px;&quot;&gt;METHOD &amp;amp; PROOF (sketch): 2N = 30 samples × 40 ns stream interval → T_input = 1.20 µs (project stream model, not full Aurora end-to-end latency) · N=15 padded to the power-of-two network M=16 → T_sort ≈ 0.50 µs (corrected anchor; 44 clk / 100 MHz = 0.44 µs analytical) · T_path ≈ L_Aurora + 1.20 + 0.50 + T_selection ≈ L_Aurora + 1.70 µs ≪ T1 → no scheduling question: layers are spatial pipelines, RMS/EDF/RR do not apply · Binding wall = LUT resources O(N·log²N): N≈128 extrapolated on Spartan-6-class — ≈70% of the CARROTS Artix-7 XC7A35T (20,800 LUT) before aggregation logic&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
